{{also|shadow-box|shadow box}}
==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|shadow-box|shadow box}}

===Etymology===
From {{com|en|shadow|box}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[diorama]] or [[shallow]] display case, usually with a glass front.
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1936|month=May|work=Chain Store Age |title=Shadowbox Tops Stairs|author=|volume=12 |number=|passage=Simply constructed of wood, a '''shadowbox''' sign frame 6 inches deep, 11 inches wide and 70 inches long is suspended over the stairway of the Scott Sotre, 124 Fifth Avenue, Jamestown, N.D.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1972 | title=The Art of Making Houses Liveable |author=Susanne Stevenson | page=174| passage=To build a '''shadowbox''' into the normal sort of hollow-core wall, we first have to make darned sure where we want the thing, for once you start making a '''shadowbox''', there's no going back unless you panel over  the whole area with a new surface.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1980 | title=Dollhouses & Dioramas|author=Robert H. Schleicher | page=102| passage=If you are going to make '''shadowboxes''' your hobby, your first consideration must be the room in which you want to place the '''shadowbox''', not the room you want to build inside the '''shadowbox'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2000 | title=Bringing Your Family History to Life Through Social History |author=Katherine Scott Sturdevant | page=80| passage=He put the '''shadowbox''' in Daddy's hands . When my father opened his eyes and recognized a display case neatly arranged with new or nearly new specimens of all of his missing World War II medals , badges , ribbons , and insignia, my father literally leapt from his seat with joy.}}
# A rectangular display area that is set off with a frame or drop shadow.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2013 | title=Origami Shadowbox Frames: Original Approach to Display Your Art|author=Yuri Shumakov; Katrin Shumakov | page=| passage=This book will show you how to make fabulous origami '''shadowbox''' frames to display your art in a beautiful and original way!}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2015| title=Computers For Seniors For Dummies |author=Nancy C. Muir | page=294| passage=Display the movie with a '''shadowbox''' effect by clicking the Aspect Ratio button.of mine Luisa Ramirez. }}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2017| title=The Trudy Silverheels Scrapbook |author=Xiomara Roma | page=88| passage=This will eventually be framed in a '''shadowbox''', I imagine.}}
# A box with a light inside used for reading X-ray images.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1962| title=Records and Briefs New York State Appellate Division |author=| page=475| passage=Q. All right. Would they be of any significance in showing the jury through a '''shadowbox'''? A. I think they helped confirm the diagnosis.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1971 | title=Personal Injury Annual |author=| page=436| passage=Q. Doctor, insofar as the condition of her back is concerned, would you be good enough to put the '''shadowbox''' up again, please?}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2003 | title=Goldstein Trial Technique - Volume 2 |author=Irving Goldstein; Fred Lane | page=!12-46| passage=To what extent is the x-ray '''shadowbox''' used in the medical profession?}}
# A shade that surrounds a lit display or screen to make it easier to read in bright environments.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1947| title=The Architects Manual of Engineered Sound Systems|author=| page=87| passage=In cases where it is difficult or impossible to reduce room illumination to this value, viewing of the projected image may be improved by providing the screen with a light shield, commonly known as a '''shadowbox''' .}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1982 | title=IEEE Conference Record--abstracts|author=| page=80| passage=A '''shadowbox''' extending 270 ° around the diode showed that the beam was reasonably uniform.}}

