===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|boxing|martial arts}} To practice moves without an actual opponent, often in front of a mirror.
#: {{ux|en|He was '''shadowboxing''' to keep fit and practice before the big fight.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1975 | title=Literature for Adolescents|author=Stephen Dunning | page=392| passage=The fighter starts to '''shadowbox''' in front of them.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2009| title=Border Songs|author=Jim Lynch | page=| passage=McAfferty giggled, then stepped back and '''shadowboxed''', jabbing the air with his little fists. }}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2018| title=Punching from the Shadows|author=Glen Sharp | page=117| passage=He '''shadowboxed''' harder than anyone I had seen before, and I soon developed that habit, too.}}
# To engage in [[evasive]] [[maneuver]]s; to avoid [[address]]ing something [[directly]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1931| title=Pagany - Volume 2, Issues 1-3 |author=| page=34| passage=He wrapped himself forever in the garden of his mind showered with golden cataclysms, sun-explosive and '''shadowboxed''' all patentcy of death.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=The Firm|passage=But, he knew, like all the other firms they had to '''shadowbox''' around the issue until things got awkward and it was apparent they had discussed everything in the world but money.|year=1991|author=John Grisham|publisher=Doubleday|location=New York|edition=1st}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2005| title=Looking Back at LBJ: White House Politics in a New Light |author=Mitchell B. Lerner | page=133| passage=The situation now clearly demanded the U.S. Army. Yet throughout the day Republican George Romney and the White House '''shadowboxed'''. }}
# {{lb|en|figuratively}} [[argue|Argue]] with an [[imaginary]] [[enemy]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1968| title=Log-exporting Problems|author=United States. Congress. Senate. Select Committee on Small Business. Subcommittee on Retailing, Distribution, and Marketing Practices | page=583| passage=Without being '''shadowboxed''' into psychedelic fears about losing Japan as a trader or as a friend — let us remind our Government today that Japan wants what we have and we want them to get what we have but not at the expense of our economy or at an unfair price.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|url=https://whatever.scalzi.com/2012/07/26/who-gets-to-be-a-geek-anyone-who-wants-to-be/#comment-344781|work=Whatever|passage=No one here is calling for Joe Peacock to be ostracized. We’re calling him on his bullshit. Brave of you to '''shadowbox''' all those non-existent censors though.|title=Who Gets To Be a Geek? Anyone Who Wants to Be|date=2012-07-28|author=Gulliver [username]|section=Comments|publisher=WordPress}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|passage=The majority of the pages in the dissent are directed at an opinion no longer in existence. Indeed much of the dissent continues to '''shadowbox''' with an opinion we never wrote.|title=Drew Adams v. School Board of St. Johns County, Florida|work=Appeals from the United States District Court for the Middle District of Florida|date=2021-07-14|author=Beverly B. Martin|page=19|id=USCA11 Case 18-13592; D.C. Docket No. 3:17-cv-00739-TJC-JBT|url=https://media.ca11.uscourts.gov/opinions/pub/files/201813592.op2.pdf}}
# To [[display]] in a shadowbox.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2004| title=Award-Winning Scrapbook Pages |author=Leisure Arts, Inc | page=42| passage=This is also the time to decide which photos will be '''shadowboxed''', which ones will be popped up, and which will lie flat on the paper.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2008| title=Tithe: A Modern Faerie Tale |author=Holly Black | page=45| passage=The trailer walls were covered with collectable plates, framed fan art, and '''shadowboxed''' phasers and tricorders.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2009| title=Create Your Own Blog|author=Tris Hussey | page=| passage=Awesome is '''shadowboxed''' images that float above the site and make your image pop off the screen.}}

